Mental Note:

Let's recap the data flow(map) of our application.
Currently, List of races with ponies resides inside my Races component. I defined the input property
raceModel in the Race component and binding it in the races template i get the list of races with ponies
in the Race component.
    races.html:

        @for (race of races; track race.id) {
        <div>
            <pr-race [raceModel]="race" />
        </div>
    }

🧠So what we are tring to achieve by creating RaceService is, relocate the race related logic from
Races component into RaceService because Angular's core design pattern is

    Component = presentation/UI
    Service = business logic + data access

Everything related to races that is NOT directly UI rendering should not reside in the component.
For example:
    getting races
    filtering races
    sorting races
    selecting featured races
    checking whether a race has started
    formatting/transforming race data
    later: calling APIs

should not live inside components, instead these logics should reside inside services because.
Services are:
    reusable
    testable
    centralized
    injectable

Now it's clear i should realocate the signal variable races containing the array of races with ponies into
the RaceService and we should get the list of races with ponies from RaceService by injecting it in my 
component

🤔Okay great!! I've created realocated the signal property 'races' into RaceService. Now in which 
component should i inject the RaceService in order to get the race list?
The answer should be obvious, we should inject the RaceService inside Races component because originally
races data were in a Race component. ⚠️⚠️And we need to remember that other components still depends on
the Races component for races data. So we just need to reallocate the races data and logic into the
RaceService and in the Races component we need to access the data and logic from RaceService by injecting
the RaceService in Races component
